    'A woman has polyuria (6 L/day) and thirst after head trauma. During a water deprivation test, urine osmolality stays low (180 mOsm/kg) while plasma osmolality rises; after desmopressin, urine osmolality rises to 650 mOsm/kg. What is the diagnosis?',
