    'A ganglion is a mucin-filled cyst arising from a joint capsule or tendon sheath, most commonly on the dorsal wrist over the scapholunate joint. It is smooth, firm, often transilluminates, and changes size with activity. Many resolve spontaneously, so observation is reasonable; aspiration has a high recurrence rate; surgical excision, including the stalk, is offered for pain, nerve compression or cosmetic concern. Giant cell tumour of the tendon sheath is a solid, non-transilluminating lump, usually on the fingers.',
